{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Ge'arta</b> — Without a bet, like the form of כריתה הנני גוער לכם את הזרע." "<b>Abadta resha'im</b> — It is tobin [i.e., the root has a vav in place of yod]." "<b>Le'olam va'ed</b> — A shortened form of לעולם ועד עולם. And because it is the end of the verse, the patah returned [to] a kamatz katan. And because of the vowel letter under the ayin, which is first, the vav is vowelized with kamatz, like הוציא לחם ויין."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {2 "The phrase 'שב הפתח קמץ קטן' is read as: the patah reverted to kamatz katan due to pausal form; 'שב' taken from the root שוב, 'returned.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:46.364429202Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}